  "code_review": {
    "owner_authority": "GET /data selects the row and returns ownerId from the same authenticated cookie user. Client adoption requires a match with /session. POST expectedOwner is an assertion only; the cookie selects the database row. Missing or mismatched owner is rejected with 409 before account_data creation or update.",
    "read_races": "A mismatched /session versus /data pair does not relabel or adopt another account's snapshot. The prior in-memory snapshot remains exportable; writes pause. For a verified changed owner whose read fails, old account data is cleared rather than exposed as the new user's.",
    "writes_versions": "The 350ms autosave waits for a pending focus revalidation. The serialized write queue, expected snapshot owner, backend version predicate and409 mapping retain conflict behavior. Error states pause later automatic writes, while dirty records remain exportable and failed dirty logout does not discard them.",
    "guest_consent": "Signed-in Agent stats read accountStorage, which excludes the legacy guest key. Guest history is read only from local browser storage when signed out or during explicit consented import. Import is replacement, not merge; ranked keys remain excluded and guest source is not deleted.",
    "size_boundary": "Guest import measures UTF-8 bytes of the complete serialized body including version, import flags, consent and expectedOwner before replacing account memory. Exactly 500,000 bytes are allowed; larger imports preserve account memory, backend snapshot and guest source. Ordinary oversize saves are rejected by the unchanged backend 500,000-byte limit and leave dirty export available.",
    "codec": "Only the account wire format is compacted. All 512 flag states and 16 optional-field combinations preserve supported record facts; legacy object arrays and unknown object fields round trip. Guest-local encoding remains unchanged, account export expands the compact representation, and the existing 3,000-row rolling limit is retained.",
    "legacy_compatibility": "Old clients without expectedOwner deliberately fail closed on writes while authenticated reads remain possible. This is not old-client write compatibility. Export-before-reload/sign-out recovery is disclosed in the PR and copy.",
    "privacy_security": "Destination, cookie authority, OAuth scope, credential persistence, deployment configuration and schema are unchanged. Test execution used synthetic users and isolated in-memory SQLite, with no real account history sent.",
    "numerical_semantics": "Fresh source inspection confirms AgentTable passes classification profileId but no registry to createAgent; its default emptyRegistry cannot select a different strategy. Integrated AgentTable also rejects villain profile candidates when building its standard HU kit. The dedicated MW3 hand path accepts no history/profile argument. The changed practice-history source affects records and classification display, not saved numerical strategies.",
    "copy": "Both 500 KB recovery messages include Chinese and Spanish translations in product-direct.json. The numerical identifiers, saved action frequencies, facts and game rules are not translated or changed."
  },
